<header><p class="st-kicker">emirate · Iberia</p><h1 class="st-title">Taifa of Badajoz</h1><p class="st-meta">1009 CE – 1094 CE (approx.) · capital Badajoz</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The great western taifa of al-Andalus, ruled by the Aftasid dynasty from Badajoz across much of what is now Extremadura and central Portugal.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After 1009 the freedman <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sabur-al-saqlabi">Sabur al-Saqlabi</a> took control of the old <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lower-march-al-andalus">Lower March</a> around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/merida-spain">Mérida</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/badajoz">Badajoz</a>. On his death in 1022 his <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vizier">vizier</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abd-allah-ibn-al-aftas">Abd Allah ibn al-Aftas</a>, of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berbers">Berber</a> descent, seized power and founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aftasid-dynasty">Aftasid dynasty</a>, which soon added <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lisbon">Lisbon</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/evora">Évora</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/santarem-portugal">Santarém</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aftasid-dynasty">Aftasids</a> governed the largest <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taifa">taifa</a> in the west, from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guadiana">Guadiana</a> valley to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tagus">Tagus</a> estuary. Their court was a literary centre: <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-al-muzaffar-of-badajoz">Muhammad al-Muzaffar</a> compiled a vast anthology, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/umar-al-mutawakkil">Umar al-Mutawakkil</a> was a noted poet. The state fought <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seville">Seville</a> over its southern borders and lost <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coimbra">Coimbra</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ferdinand-i-of-leon">Ferdinand I of León</a> in 1064, then paid tribute to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-castile">Castile</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1093 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/umar-al-mutawakkil">al-Mutawakkil</a> ceded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lisbon">Lisbon</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sintra">Sintra</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/santarem-portugal">Santarém</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alfonso-vi-of-castile">Alfonso VI</a> in return for protection. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almoravid-empire">Almoravids</a> saw this as treason, took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/badajoz">Badajoz</a> in 1094 and executed him with his sons, ending the dynasty.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/taifa-of-badajoz.jpg" alt="Taifa of Badajoz" width="320" height="271"><figcaption>Image: Tyk · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Location_map_Taifa_of_Badajoz.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1009 CE – 1094 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>emirate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Badajoz</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Abd Allah ibn al-Aftas, Muhammad al-Muzaffar, Umar al-Mutawakkil</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Andalusi Arabic, Mozarabic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/spain">Spain</a>, <a href="/countries/portugal">Portugal</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Aftasid Kingdom of Badajoz</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1052&amp;focus=taifa-of-badajoz" aria-label="Taifa of Badajoz on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4507 783 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Taifa of Badajoz lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M4827 1039L4881 1071M4827 1039L4809 1080M4827 1039L4799 1289M4827 1039L4773 1045"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4881 1071h0M4809 1080h0M4799 1289h0M4773 1045h0"